IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb1-nouns`
IMPORT `cb1-part4-isc-register`

-- Tests of cb1-part4-isc-register.l4 (s 21.1 to s 21.4). Expected values are written from the text of the
-- Act (src:302-417), never from the code's output: each comment says what the text gives.

§ `Tests -- Part IV register of individuals with significant control`

§§ `s 21.1(1) the register`

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
      b IS A BOOLEAN
      c IS A BOOLEAN
      d IS A BOOLEAN
      e IS A BOOLEAN
      f IS A BOOLEAN
      g IS A BOOLEAN
      h IS A BOOLEAN
      i IS A BOOLEAN
      j IS A BOOLEAN
      k IS A BOOLEAN
      l IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Register of individuals with significant control as kept (s 21.1(1))`
`a register` a b c d e f g h i j k l MEANS
    `Register of individuals with significant control as kept (s 21.1(1))` WITH
        `the register is kept at the registered office or at another place in Canada designated by the directors` IS a
        `it contains the name and date of birth of each individual with significant control` IS b
        `it contains the residential address of each individual with significant control` IS c
        `an address for service has been provided to the corporation` IS d
        `it contains the address for service of each individual with significant control` IS e
        `it contains the citizenship of each individual with significant control` IS f
        `it contains the jurisdiction of residence for tax purposes of each individual with significant control` IS g
        `it contains the day on which each individual became or ceased to be an individual with significant control` IS h
        `it contains a description of how each individual is an individual with significant control over the corporation, including a description of their interests and rights in respect of shares` IS i
        `there is other prescribed information` IS j
        `it contains the other prescribed information` IS k
        `it contains a description of each step taken in accordance with subsection 21.1(2)` IS l

-- src:302-312: everything required, with an address for service provided and prescribed information existing
#ASSERT `the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- no address for service was provided, so none is required; no other prescribed information exists
#ASSERT `the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- an address for service was provided but the register lacks it
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
-- other prescribed information exists but the register lacks it
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE))
-- each other item, one at a time
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the register contains what s 21.1(1) requires` (`a register` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))

